            <ArticleTitle>[Struma as a cause of a brachialgia].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>534-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 76-year-old woman with a great multi-nodular goitre and no neurological deficits suffered from increasing pain of the lateral upper arm. A combination of nerve blockades and physical measures was not effective in terms of continuous pain control. Subtotal thyroidectomy resulted in a long-term complete pain relief. The underlying mechanism is explained as a compression of the superior trunk of brachial plexus by a goitre. In future a goitre should be taken into consideration in the aetiology of a brachialgia.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
